                                    ELB
                            Elastic Load Balancer

--> ELB automatically monitor and distribute incoming web traffic among the avaibale servers.

--> types of ELB:
1. Application LB:
---> HTTP and HTTPS traffic 
---> path based routing
---> works on 7th layer of OSI model (Application layer) 

2. Network LB:
---> TCP, UDP Protocol
---> handle million requests per second
---> ultra low latency
---> works on 4th layer of OSI model (Transport Layer)

3. Gateway LB:
---> third party security applience
---> works on 3rd layer of OSI model (Networl Layer)

4. Classic LB: prev gen

** Target Group:
--> A Target Group is a collection of backend resources where the Load Balancer sends client traffic.

** Listners:
--> A Listener is a process on the Load Balancer that checks for incoming connection requests on a specific protocol and port.




